 5. ☎️ Trump&#x27;s &quot;tough&quot; call with Bibi 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump talks to reporters during a Halloween party in Mar-a-Lago's ballroom on Saturday night. Photo: Doug Mills/The New York Times President Trump had a candid phone call with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu Saturday about the state of U.S. negotiations with Iran and how quickly to return to combat, Axios' Barak Ravid writes. 

 Why it matters: The sources said Netanyahu is pressing Trump to strike Iran immediately after the midterm elections tomorrow. But Trump, for now, wants to let negotiations play out — a strategy Netanyahu is concerned about. The Israeli source said the call was "tough," while the U.S. source described it as "direct."

 Trump is pursuing dual tracks — trying to reach a deal to restart peace talks while also preparing for a possible resumption of major combat operations after the midterms. Trump told reporters on Saturday that negotiations with Iran are "going fine" and noted he is not "in much of a hurry." Share this story . 

 
 
