 8. 🗽 1 fun thing: 60,000 runners 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A runner dressed as Superman crosses the Verrazzano–Narrows Bridge at the start of the New York City Marathon yesterday. Photo: Brendan McDermid/Reuters Nearly 60,000 runners from 140+ countries ran the New York City Marathon yesterday.

 It's the 50th year the course snaked through all five boroughs — starting in Staten Island and ending in Central Park. An estimated 2 million spectators lined the streets. Photo: Hiroko Masuike/The New York Times Above: Runners pound Brooklyn's pavement.

